The license above covers Code X-Ray's own code. The extension package also
bundles the components below, each under its own license (texts and notices
in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and in the extension's dist/kitten folder). The
sizes are what each adds to the installed extension and to the download.

- Extension code, pages and icons: Code X-Ray (MIT).
  2.4 MB installed, 1.0 MB of the download.
- Analyses of TypeScript and JavaScript: TypeScript compiler 6.0.3 (Apache-2.0).
  23.2 MB installed, 4.4 MB of the download.
- C# support: tree-sitter and tree-sitter-c-sharp (MIT).
  5.8 MB installed, 0.4 MB of the download.
- Natural voices and the code model: the model runtime: ONNX Runtime Web 1.24.3, by Microsoft (MIT).
  11.9 MB installed, 3.0 MB of the download.
- Natural voices: pronunciation and the voice engine: eSpeak NG via phonemizer.js 1.2.1 (GPL-3.0, Apache-2.0).
  1.3 MB installed, 0.7 MB of the download.

Total: about 44.7 MB installed, a 9.5 MB download. eSpeak NG (GPL-3.0) runs as
a separate program, dist/kitten/phonemize.mjs, with the GPL text and a source
notice next to it.

Not bundled, downloaded from Hugging Face only when you choose them, into the
extension's storage, each under its own license:

- Git reel natural voices: one Kitten TTS 0.8 model, by KittenML / Stellon Labs
  (Apache-2.0): Nano int8 27.6 MB (recommended), Nano 60.0 MB, Micro 44.7 MB or
  Mini 81.5 MB. Chosen with the setting tsStructure.reel.voiceModel.
- Git reel code model: all-MiniLM-L6-v2 (Apache-2.0, by the
  sentence-transformers team; int8 ONNX export by Xenova), 23.2 MB. Turned off
  with the setting tsStructure.reel.codeModel.

Every library and model is credited on the Credits page of Code X-Ray Settings.
